From 0e8cb05684102d5610aa7bb0879f30784e518e9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Savek-CC <me@home>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 18:03:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] TK: Retry pump status with a backoff after an error or
 suspend

While the pump accepts commands the loop keeps it connected on its own. Once it
stops (error, empty battery, occlusion, out of range) the loop goes quiet as
well, so the status read from KeepAlive is the only thing left to notice that
the user fixed the pump.

Requesting it every 5 min for hours is wasteful, so recovery attempts are spaced
5, 10, 15 and then 30 min apart, measured from the later of last contact and
last attempt, and reset as soon as the pump answers. A suspended pump enters
recovery immediately instead of waiting for the 15 min staleness threshold.

One attempt is one readStatus; the connection retrying inside an attempt stays
with the command queue.
